# team/config/dashboard_windows.census
#
# Single source of truth for the tmux dashboard's window and pane layout.
# team/scripts/dashboard/create.sh is what actually BUILDS the session;
# this file is what DESCRIBES it, machine-readably, so the description can
# never quietly drift from the build. Everything derived from the board
# shape — create.sh's "Window order" comment block, docs/DASHBOARD-PANES.md's
# per-window tables, and the pytest suite's window/pane expectations — reads
# THIS file through one reader per language (team/scripts/lib/
# dashboard_window_census.sh for bash, team/pgai_agent_kanban/dashboard/
# window_census.py for Python) instead of hand-transcribing the window list.
# team/scripts/dashboard/generate_window_docs.py renders the derived
# surfaces from this file and, in --check mode, refuses when a derived
# surface disagrees with what this file says the board looks like.
#
# Format: tab-separated values, one record per data line. Order is
# significant — windows appear in tmux creation order, and each window's
# pane records appear in tmux pane-index order directly after it.
#
# Parse rule: a line is a DATA line only when its first tab-delimited field
# is exactly "W" or "P". Every other line — blank, or starting with
# anything else, including this header block — is a comment and MUST be
# ignored by readers. '#' is used for comments here purely by convention
# (matching team/config/default_palette.txt); readers must not special-case
# '#' itself, only the "first field is W or P" rule.
#
# W (window) record — 5 fields after the sigil:
#   W  <tmux_index>  <name>  <variant>  <pane_count>
#
#   tmux_index  0-based tmux window index, in the order create.sh's
#               `tmux new-session` / `tmux new-window` calls run. No
#               base-index override exists in create.sh (verified: no
#               `base-index` setting anywhere in the tree), so this is the
#               literal index `tmux list-windows` reports.
#   name        The tmux window name create.sh passes to -n / -s. The
#               per-project drill windows are dynamic (one is created per
#               projects.cfg entry, renamed to "drill-N: <project>" after
#               creation) — both drill records use the literal placeholder
#               name "drill-N" rather than a real project-specific name.
#   variant     "-" for windows with exactly one layout. The drill window
#               has two mutually exclusive layouts selected by the
#               project's workflow_type (create.sh reads
#               [project] workflow_type from each project's project.cfg):
#               "release" (5 panes, shared by the release and feature
#               workflow types) and "document" (2 panes). Both drill
#               variants share tmux_index 14 — real installs place drill-1,
#               drill-2, ... at indices 14, 15, ... depending on how many
#               projects are registered; this census describes the
#               PER-WINDOW pane template, not a specific installation's
#               project count.
#   pane_count  Number of P records that must follow for this window.
#               generate_window_docs.py --check treats a mismatch between
#               this count and the number of P records actually present as
#               a malformed census (refuses loud; never silently truncates
#               or pads the pane list).
#
# P (pane) record — 6 fields after the sigil, immediately following its
# window's W record (each P record followed by its C record, below):
#   P  <tmux_index>  <variant>  <pane_seq>  <position>  <script>  <standalone_cmd>
#
#   tmux_index    Must match the W record's tmux_index directly above it.
#   variant       Must match the W record's variant directly above it.
#   pane_seq      0-based tmux pane index within the window (the number
#                 after the "." in a `session:window.pane` tmux target).
#   position      Human-readable position/size label — the same text
#                 docs/DASHBOARD-PANES.md's "Pane position" column carries
#                 (e.g. "Top (HEADER, ~11%)"). Free text; not machine-
#                 parsed beyond being one TSV field.
#   script        The script (relative to team/scripts/dashboard/) that
#                 populates the pane, or a parenthesized note for panes no
#                 script populates (an interactive shell).
#   standalone_cmd The exact command an operator runs from a plain shell to
#                 reproduce the pane's output once, outside tmux. "N/A --
#                 ..." for panes with no standalone equivalent.
#
# C (cadence) record — 5 fields after the sigil, directly after the P
# record it describes; every P record has exactly one:
#   C  <tmux_index>  <variant>  <pane_seq>  <cadence>  <when_hidden>
#
#   tmux_index,   Identify the pane, exactly as in its P record.
#   variant,
#   pane_seq
#   cadence       How often the pane refreshes while visible: a whole
#                 number of seconds; "refresh" for [dashboard]
#                 refresh_seconds (default 5); "stream" for a renderer
#                 that never returns, run under cadence-loop.sh --stream
#                 (visibility re-checked every refresh_seconds); "-" for
#                 a pane with no refresh loop (an interactive shell).
#   when_hidden   What the pane does while it is not visible (its window
#                 is not active, or no client is attached): "pause" -- it
#                 does no work (no renders; a stream is stopped) -- or
#                 "always-on" -- it keeps refreshing. "always-on" is
#                 reserved for the one status surface in window 0 and is
#                 accepted nowhere else. A pane with no refresh loop
#                 declares "pause": it does nothing on its own.
#   team/scripts/dashboard/lint_pane_refresh_cadence.py checks that every
#   pane declares one of the two (via window_census.py's
#   pane_hidden_declaration_findings), and lib/cadence.sh is what makes a
#   "pause" pane pause.
#
# Reading in bash:
#   while IFS=$'\t' read -r kind a b c d e f; do
#       [[ "$kind" == "W" || "$kind" == "P" ]] || continue
#       # W: a=tmux_index b=name       c=variant d=pane_count
#       # P: a=tmux_index b=variant    c=pane_seq d=position e=script f=standalone_cmd
#   done < team/config/dashboard_windows.census
#
# Reading in Python: see team/pgai_agent_kanban/dashboard/window_census.py
# (load_census()) -- do not hand-parse this file a second time.
#
# Do not duplicate this list elsewhere. Consumers read this file; they do
# not hand-transcribe the window/pane list into create.sh comments, docs, or
# test fixtures.


W	0	main	-	4
P	0	-	0	Top (HEADER, ~11%, floored to fit the full cron roster)	show-multi.sh	show-multi.sh --mode header --kanban-root $PGAI_AGENT_KANBAN_ROOT_PATH
C	0	-	0	refresh	pause
P	0	-	1	Bottom (LOGS, ~40%)	logs.sh	logs.sh --kanban-root $PGAI_AGENT_KANBAN_ROOT_PATH --stdout
C	0	-	1	stream	pause
P	0	-	2	Middle (PROGRESS, full width of left column)	show-multi.sh	show-multi.sh --mode progress --kanban-root $PGAI_AGENT_KANBAN_ROOT_PATH
C	0	-	2	refresh	pause
P	0	-	3	Right (QUEUES, ~25% of window, full height)	show-multi.sh	show-multi.sh --mode queues --kanban-root $PGAI_AGENT_KANBAN_ROOT_PATH
C	0	-	3	refresh	pause

